Keep video transfers small and never drop one the kernel refuses.

libuvc 0.0.8 queues 100 isochronous transfers of up to 32 packets each, about 96 KB per transfer
for a typical USB 2 camera. The kernel needs one physically contiguous buffer per transfer, and a
phone that is short of memory refuses blocks that large with ENOMEM. libuvc then freed the refused
transfer, or, if the very first one failed, all of them while still reporting success. The stream
lost its transfers one by one and went quiet with no error.

This caps each transfer at 32 KB, parks a refused or failed transfer instead of freeing it, adds
uvc_retry_parked_transfers() for the event thread to queue parked transfers again, and frees parked
transfers when the stream stops. uvc_submit_hook lets tests make submissions fail.

